  "title": "Critique: feedback is not only modulatory",
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "d96d736a-5d63-447f-9673-4811ae827edf",
      "text": "Apical accounts assume that feedforward signals drive and feedback signals modulate. Evidence on class 1 and class 2 synapses contradicts that assumption, since feedforward modulation and feedback drive are also common, and whether class follows dendritic site is unknown.",
